Track 2: "Who Spooled the Wire Recorder, Jesse?"
- Story & Context: Hidden in a rusted Airstream trailer behind the frozen Ferris wheel in Hopkinsville during the 2017 totality, recording engineer Martha Crane broke down during an unhinged session of Wurlitzer improvisations, confessing on magnetic wire that she had intentionally sabotaged the carnival's power grid for a decade to force extended blackout sets. The stifling room reeked of overheating selenium rectifiers and stale menthol smoke as her trembling fingers struck unresolved minor ninth chords that buzzed against the trailer’s aluminum walls. Outside, stranded midway patrons pressed their ears against the exterior rivets, overhearing her broken falsetto deliver the confession: "I stole the sparks so your ghost could dance with mine." The take was preserved directly from the magnetic wire, complete with her weeping softly between the tremolo pulses.
