Track 3: Daguerre-Crawl (Omen of the Cold Sun)
- Story & Context: Decades after the nomadic carnival vanished into regional myth, audio preservationists exploring the sunken mud of Bombay Beach unearthed a glass-plate sound cartridge fused to the motor of a drowned carousel organ. Legend held that during the final four minutes of the Great American Eclipse, The Syzygy Arcade played this circular, hypnotic gospel-funk progression and walked off the midway into the white salt flats, leaving their keyboards to drone unattended. When digital archivists finally coaxed the degraded audio from the glass disc, it yielded a sluggish, narcotic groove layered with tape hiss, culminating in Judith’s spectral hook: "Leave the ferris wheel turning for nobody at all." Playing the recovered master file is said to cause vintage vacuum tubes to hum in spontaneous resonance.
